# Auto detect text files, LF in the repository AND in every working copy: Prettier checks
# for LF, and a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true used to get CRLF — after main was
# taken from a bundle, 31 files there failed `prettier --check` with no change of their own.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The launchers (1.6.0): shell scripts must keep LF even in a Windows checkout — a CRLF
# start.sh copied to a Mac or Linux (the flash copy) fails with "bad interpreter";
# cmd.exe wants CRLF for its labels.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.command text eol=lf
*.cmd     text eol=crlf
